The sterilizer is manufactured in accordance with the relevant provisions of technical specifications such as GB/T 150-2011 “Pressure Vessels” and “TSG 21-2016 Safety Technical Supervision Regulations for Fixed Pressure Vessels”.
Before starting the machine every day, check whether the electrical components of the sterilizer are normal, whether the mechanical structure is damaged, whether the safety interlocking device is abnormal, etc., and everything is normal before it can be powered on.
At the end of the sterilization every day, the lock power button on the front door of the sterilizer should be turned off, the power circuit breaker on the building should be disconnected, and the water source shut-off valve should be closed. The sterilizer should be kept clean.
The accumulated water in the sterilizer should be removed every day to prevent the accumulated scale from affecting the normal heating of the electric heating tube and affecting the steam quality, and at the same time affecting the sterilization effect.
The service life of the sterilizer is about 10 years, and the production date is shown on the product nameplate; if the user needs to continue using the product that has reached the designed service life, he should apply to the registration authority for a change in the registration certificate.
