Farming Is The Biggest Thing In The World
In order to reduce the damage caused by insect pests to crops, we have produced a large number of different insecticides. The mechanism of action of various insecticides is the same, so how do we choose the ones that are really suitable for our crops?
We farmers are very familiar with imidacloprid, so thiamethoxam is a new insecticidal star. What are its advantages over the older generation?
The activity of the hydroxylated metabolites of imidacloprid was reduced.
Studies have shown that Thiamethoxam can activate plant stress resistance proteins, and at the same time produce auxin, cytokinin, gibberellin, abscisic acid, peroxidase, polyphenol oxidase, and phenylalanine ammonia lyase in plants. As a result, thiamethoxam in turn makes crop stems and roots more robust and enhances stress resistance.
Thiamethoxam has strong leaf conduction activity and root systemic properties, and the agent can be quickly and fully absorbed.
★Citrus diseases are sprayed about 2 times in each of the spring shoot growth period, summer shoot growth period, young fruit period and autumn shoot growth period, which can effectively control the occurrence and damage of boils, anthracnose, macular disease and scab;For ponkan varieties, it is necessary to spray 1-2 times at the early stage of fruit color change.
When preventing and controlling brown spot and powdery mildew, start spraying from the initial stage of the disease, once every 10-15 days, and spray 2~3 times continuously;
★Spray the strawberry powdery mildew and brown spot from the beginning of the disease, and spray 2~3 times once every 10~15 days.
★Peach, plum, and apricot diseases should be sprayed from 20 to 30 days after flowering, once every 10 to 15 days, for 3 to 5 consecutive sprays, which can effectively prevent scab, anthracnose and fungal perforation.
From the end of June, continue to spray, once every 10 to 15 days, and spray 4 to 6 times, which can effectively prevent and control rust, anthracnose, ring disease and fruit spot disease.
★For pear diseases, spray once before and after blooming to effectively prevent rust and control the formation of black star diseased tips. From then on, start spraying when black star disease diseased tips or leaves are first seen, once every 10-15 days It can be used alternately with different types of agents and spray continuously for 5-8 times to effectively prevent black spot disease, and also prevent black spot, anthracnose, ring spot, brown spot and powdery mildew.
★Spray for banana leaf spot and scab from the early stage of the disease or when the spot is first seen, once every 10 to 15 days, and spray for 3 to 4 times in a row.
