This is a prior permit granted by the country of destination through its consulate or embassy in the country of origin. There are different types of visas, and it will depend on how long you plan to stay, choosing one or the other.
4 Which are the countries that require a visa for a Spanish citizen?
8 What is my visa number?
The only requirement is that stay must be longer than 90 days (three months).
Residence: if you come to work (self-employed or employed) or to stay and live.
Which are the countries that require a visa for a Spanish citizen?
The tourist visa, also known as B2, is the document you need to travel to a country. It will help you sightseeing, visiting family or friends, or for medical treatment; instead, you will not be able to use it to work.
To request it, You have to go to the embassy or consulate of the destination country in your country of origin. Take with you a photograph of yourself showing your face and your passport.
It is rare, but it really depends on each case. To avoid this, try to convince the consulate officer that, first, you don't plan to stay and live and second that you have enough resources.
If you deliver everything by hand and it turns out that the required documents are correct, it usually takes no more than five business days. It is not much, and you can take advantage of it to plan your trip.
Once you have it, you will probably wonder what the visa number is, since these cards have a large number of numbers that have their own characteristics, so let's see how we can quickly recognize it.
