The beaches in Martinique Author: FRENCH INTERFACE Published Date: 24 November 2019 Leave a Comment The beaches are in Martinique
Many say that the most beautiful beaches in Martinique are located in the south of the island.
Around the charming village of Anses d'Arlet, you will also find a multitude of pristine beaches, ideal for relaxing.
but above, do not overlook the Atlantic coast and the north of the island.
From the Caribbean to the Atlantic Ocean, planning your trip to Martinique discovering the most beautiful jewels of its coastline.
What a joy to swim in Martinique in fresh water all year round !
The pleasant sea temperature also offers the more athletic many possibilities for activities : dives, surfing and other nautical activities.
For surfers, meet at the end of the Caravelle peninsula on the "Surfeurs" beach or Anse Dufour, beach with waves suitable for all levels.
If you are looking for the best beach in Martinique, is at Anse snake you find it.
In the tropical humidity, the beach is swept by powerful rollers of the Caribbean Sea.
It's just a real moment of happiness !
The second allows to plunge into the turquoise waters, enjoying white sand.
And icing on the cake, you are in one of the best locations in Martinique where observe sea turtles.
Since the dock overlooking the turquoise sea, the view of the church and Creole houses of the village is absolutely sublime.
Rising from the waters of the Caribbean Sea, Diamond Rock is a true symbol of Martinique.
But pay attention to the heavy swell which can make swimming dangerous.
In large shaded part, it is ideal for families with children.
To avoid the crowds, Come preferably early morning or late afternoon.
Remember to bring plenty of water, a pair of shoes and your supplies for the day.
You can access it by car on a stony road but you have to cross a private road with an entrance fee to 2,50 Euro and input schedules between 8 am and 16h.
The beach is very pleasant, very wide and lined with trees for sun protection.
The sea is regularly a little rough but still pleasant for swimming.
The whites of François Fund are accessible only by kayak or boat during a day trip where one offers swimming, Creole lunch, ti-punch in a pleasant atmosphere.
These sandy shoals are located between the islet Oscar and Thierry islet where you can bathe in one meter of water.
Rather come in the morning because at noon, it's fast bottling between motor boats, catamarans and canoes coming from all sides.
The Caravelle peninsula is a place apart on the Martinique coast.
Located south of the village after the fishing port, Pointe du Faula is a huge expanse of grass and sand whose characteristic is a sandy bottom covered with only fifteen centimeters of water that you can get away with more 400 meters out and join the Whites walking Fund.
Many trees line the beach for sun protection.
Located Atlantic side of the island, Cape Macré the beach is one of the most beautiful beaches of the island with a very calm water due to a coral reef that protects waves.
Attention to children because the beach falls steeply into the sea and one quickly loses foot.
After a twenty minute walk on a nice trail, you arrive in paradise at Anse Grosse Roche.
Many coconut trees lining the white sand beach and provide shaded areas for sun protection.
The Michel bay is conducive to family swim.
therefore it is ideal for parents with young children.
long 27 km, it is the longest hiking the island along the southern coast overlooking beautiful beaches.
This hike can be cut in 5 sections.
uncrowded, yet it is a beautiful beach with crystal clear water and calm.
