If you think starting a video by asking for a subscription makes you come across as being sales-y, you can do so at the end of the video. Don’t forget to demonstrate why your channel is worth subscribing to and the content you bring to the table for your viewers’ benefit.
This may seem like a no-brainer but still needs to be mentioned. Far too many novice YouTube creators feel they can become the next big YouTube sensation by posting average content.
Remember to do extensive groundwork before you think of creating your next video. Rather than re-making what everyone else in your industry is making, think out-of-the-box and come up with your unique content ideas.
One that posts once in a month only to go AWOL?
We all know the answer – we choose the one who is regularly updating their channel with new content for their viewers. As a creator, your audience expects you to post on time to keep them engaged and attract new viewers as well.
Content creators on YouTube can add a small watermark to all the videos they create. Quite often beginner content creators don’t even realize the watermark option exists on the platform.
An excellent way to gain free YouTube subscribers is by getting your viewers excited and addicted to the content you make. Because, once they like what they see, your work will do all the talking, and they will stick around for more.
Whatever be it, remember to entice your audience by giving them a hint of what your next video is going to be about. If you do your job well enough, you can be sure your loyal viewers will be present to watch the next video with bated breath and give you free YouTube likes.
Create Playlists to Keep Your Viewers Hooked
Perhaps you offer accounting lessons and cover one topic each in one video. Or, you have a set of webinars?
To add an end screen, simply go to the left menu of Creator Studio and click Content. Choose the video you want to add the end screen to.
Don’t Forget to Interact with Your Viewers
When you hear their suggestions and act on them, they feel heard and relate to your content more. Remember, happy viewers can bring more viewers by word-of-mouth publicity and sharing your content with their circle of friends.
These are like movie trailers that give a sneak-peak into what you do and the content you create for your viewers. You can use channel trailers to highlight the benefits of your channel.
Whatever works for you and agrees with your line of work. Make it impactful so the viewers can be converted into subscribers with ease.
YouTube also creates a default thumbnail for videos by simply snagging a random screenshot from it. In most cases, this isn’t good enough to drive traffic to your video and prompt the viewer to click.
It’s also quite possible that you may have a similar audience. Why not leverage each other’s viewers by joining hands and benefiting from each other?
Collaborating with influencers to grab more eyeballs for your channel is probably the oldest trick in the marketing book and yet never fails to work its magic. When your audience sees such collaborations, it can further trigger more recommendations or ideas in their minds.
An increasing number of apps such as Instagram and Facebook are getting this feature which is making it easier for brands to get on board. From interesting Q&A sessions and webinars to live tutorials and product demonstrations, there are countless things you can explore on a YouTube live to gain free YouTube subscribers.
