The living room is usually the room with the largest dimensions of the house. But even when it is small, the color chosen to paint the room will have a great impact and influence on your overall character.
Color in addition to contributing to enhance a specific decorative style in the living room, it will influence the atmosphere of the room. So the first thing you should ask yourself is how you want to use the room and how you can use color to your advantage.
White is a luminous color that allows us to play with different colors and adopt different decorative styles without limiting ourselves. Nails White walls They combine with any type of floor and give all the prominence to the furniture, so they are always an excellent alternative.
To function as a backdrop in spaces where the furniture is responsible for providing that modern touch that we are looking for, always through soft but well-defined lines. Gray walls
These tones also contribute to giving prominence to both the furniture and the works of art that you may have in the living room. A white sofa will highlight the gray color on the walls and at the same time provide a modern and elegant atmosphere, while one in pastel colors will provide a more familiar and relaxed atmosphere.
Both in some and in the others if our only fear of betting on gray is that these spaces may be cold, we only have to make sure to accompany these colors with others that raise the temperature. and that's where materials such as wood and leather They become great allies.
What a priori could be an attractive alternative could ruin a space. That is why at Decoora we encourage you to bet on black in moderation.
