Wood is very sensitive to moisture, which is why specific care for it is very important. Extending the life of the wood in the bathroom will depend to a large extent on the cleaning and good maintenance that you carry out almost daily.
In the vast majority of cases, the wood used in the bathroom is usually teak or larch. In the first case, it is a tropical and waterproof wood.
Despite being quite waterproof, we must not forget that wood is a very delicate material and it is important to follow a series of tips or guidelines when keeping them in perfect condition.
Ultimately, wood is an ideal material to use in the bathroom.
